Design and protocol references
------------------------------

No third-party source code is vendored in this tree. The following informed the
design and were read as documentation rather than copied:

  ArduPilot IOMCU     the two-processor split and the watchdog ratio
  YGE                 the OpenYGE material the specification here is written
                      from
  BLHeli / BLHeli_S, AM32, ESCape32, VESC, Hitec
                      published protocol descriptions and configurator
                      behaviour
  heeen/supvan-cups   the print protocol of Supvan T50-series label
                      printers (docs/PROTOCOL.md and the record and buffer
                      layouts of crates/supvan-proto), reverse-engineered
                      by that project from the vendor's app; MIT License.
                      protocols/supvan is written from that description and
                      from captures of the station's printer

Every protocol implementation here is written from a published specification
or, where none is published, from captures of the wire, rather than from
another implementation, because nearly every open implementation of these
protocols is GPL or AGPL against this repository's MIT. The programming
protocol of KST and Chaservo servos has no published specification: it is the
one written from wire captures (see Trademarks below).

test/host/greatest.h is a 107-line test harness written for this project. It is
not the `greatest` library of the same name.


